# Windows hosts running the user-session sshd -- see
# .chezmoiscripts/00-nt/035-sshd-user-session and the README. That sshd runs
# inside the interactive desktop session rather than as the stock SYSTEM
# service, which is what makes mapped drive letters (B:, Y:, Z:) visible over
# scp; the port is nonstandard because the stock service is disabled rather
# than removed, so nothing has to be reconciled if a Windows feature update
# quietly puts it back on 22.
#
# Templated purely so the port stays sourced from .chezmoidata/sshd.toml
# instead of being duplicated here and silently drifting.
#
# User and identity come from the defaults in ../config: `Host *` sets
# User regulad, which `Match User regulad` tags rsa3072.

Host winlite
    HostName winlite.tail11540.ts.net
    Port {{ .sshd.port }}
